  "details": "I for example use a Rift S (which is not capable of finger tracking), and most people aren't using finger-tracked setups and probably don't even want this regardless.  I know VRChat can detect if you are using touch controllers or vive wands for example, why should they be forced to have to find and disable the setting for their awkwardly posed hands that override the avatar's gestures?\n\nThe whole input 2.0 update was not thought out at all.  Please consider the implications before forcing a, in a way breaking, major change like this to the platform. I know countless people are completely confused and bothered by this sudden and unexpected change, especially when it's a bother to likely most users.",
